{"availability":"available","full":"jhoenicke/seahaven","name":"seahaven","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Lean","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2021-04-19T10:50:50Z","updated":"2026-09-14T22:19:44Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://jhoenicke.de/seahaven/online.html","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:04:47.612Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:04:47.612Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:04:47.612Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:50.809Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:45:04.143Z","stars":1,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:04:47.612Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The cards are initially dealt out into 10 tableau piles holding 5 cards each and the remaining two cards are dealt to the reserved cells. There are four reserved cells total, each can hold at most one card. The object of the game is to move all cards to the foundations (at top left and right) from Ace to King by following suits.","On the tableau piles you can build down from King to Ace following suit, the reserved cells can hold any card, but only one. Empty tableau piles may hold kings. You can move the cards only one by one. Only the lowest card from the tableau piles and the cards on reserved cells are available.","You just have to say which card to move, and the program will automatically determine the destination: the foundations, a tableau pile, or the reserved cells, in that order."],"features":["None: Only the lowest card of the clicked pile is moved and","Flutes: When moving cards from the tableau piles it will move all","Aces: It will also move all cards to the foundations as soon as","Full: It will also move all matching cards from the reserved cells"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jhoenicke/seahaven/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"946393e2b2ca0d11a50035a2b7e4ab71d732b981afd3e04612c